The four-act drill is complete. Summary:

## 1 · Diagnose — `agent-output/H8-fire-drill/diagnosis.md`
Ran the unmodified trio in an isolated profile against the 0.1.2-alpha.2 host and found one boot-blocking failure plus two latent ones:

| Plugin | Breakage | Card |
|---|---|---|
| `drill-host` | `inject: ["apiProxy"]` — service/package deleted; entry stays `pending` and the whole tree aborts | **DSH-0.1.2-A1-01** |
| `drill-host` | `ctx.apiProxy.llm.providers()` call site; decoy comment says "switch to `remote`" — but `remote` is **client-plane only** (measured: `pending (waiting for service: remote)`) | **DSH-0.1.2-A1-01** |
| `drill-host` | dead dependency on `@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-apiproxy` (no 0.1.2 line on npm) | **A1-01** + **R-01** |
| `drill-web` | raw `ctx.webServer.register('/ping')` bypasses the unified browser gate (host webserver has no auth by design) | **DSH-0.1.2-A1-08** |
| `drill-tools` | `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools@^0.1.2-alpha.1` — alpha.1 was GitHub-only (exact 404); the caret silently floats to a later cohort member | **R-01**, **R-08** |

## 2 · Fix — `/app/fixture/` edited directly
- `drill-host`: `inject = ["llm"]`, `ctx.llm.listProviders()`, stale dependency removed.
- `drill-web`: keeps `webServer` + `/ping` protocol, adds `connection` to inject and guards the handler with `ctx.connection.requestRejection(req)` before any side effect.
- `drill-tools`: cohort floor rewritten to `^0.1.2-alpha.2` (published target).

## 3 · Deploy — `agent-output/H8-fire-drill/smoke.md` (+ raw `evidence*/`)
Isolated `DSH_HOME`, profile `web`, all three installed, cold boot, token→cookie exchange, then `/ping`: **401** unauthenticated, **303 + Set-Cookie** on `GET /?token=<redacted> **200 `pong`** with the cookie, **401** forged cookie, **403** foreign `Host`. No `pending` entries; `host_exit=0`. Reproduced three ways (link install, post-bump, and packed-tarball consumer install).

## 4 · Release — `agent-output/H8-fire-drill/release.md`
All three bumped `0.1.0 → 0.2.0-alpha.1` (own SemVer, not the host version); packed artifacts validated and consumer-installed. The checklist lists the six gate layers and answers the routing rule: **a prerelease must go to a project-declared non-`latest` dist-tag (`next`), never `latest`**; no `--force`, no skipped checks — the README's `pnpm publish --force` procedure is explicitly rejected. Nothing was published. Throwaway profiles/caches were removed; only the fixture edits and `agent-output/` remain.

